Sec. 1 (adding A.R.S. 44-7862, subsection A, introduction): {+A. A FIREARMS DEALER THAT TRANSFERS FIREARMS TO PERSONS IN THIS STATE SHALL TAKE REASONABLE MEASURES TO PREVENT THE TRANSFER OF FIREARMS TO STRAW PURCHASERS OR FIREARMS TRAFFICKERS, INCLUDING:+}
Sec. 1 (A.R.S. 44-7862, subsection A, paragraph 6): {+6. LIMITING TRANSFERS OF FIREARMS TO ONE TRANSFER EVERY THIRTY DAYS PER CIVILIAN CUSTOMER WHO IS NOT A LAW ENFORCEMENT OFFICER.+}
Sec. 1 (A.R.S. 44-7862, subsection B, paragraph 1): {+1. REFUSING TO TRANSFER A FIREARM UNTIL A BACKGROUND CHECK HAS BEEN COMPLETED AND THE TRANSFEREE IS CLEARED TO PURCHASE THE FIREARM.+}
Sec. 1 (A.R.S. 44-7862, subsection B, paragraph 5): {+5. REFUSING TO SELL FIREARMS AT FIREARMS SHOWS UNLESS ALL FIREARMS TRANSFERS AT THE SHOWS ARE CONDUCTED ONLY ON COMPLETION OF A BACKGROUND CHECK.+}
Sec. 1 (A.R.S. 44-7862, subsection B, paragraph 6): {+6. PERFORMING BACKGROUND CHECKS FOR PRIVATE SELLERS FOR A REASONABLE FEE.+}
Sec. 1 (A.R.S. 44-7862, subsection C, paragraph 5): {+5. LIMITING PURCHASES OF FIREARMS TO ONE PURCHASE EVERY THIRTY DAYS PER CIVILIAN CUSTOMER WHO IS NOT A LAW ENFORCEMENT OFFICER.+}
Sec. 1 (A.R.S. 44-7862, subsection F, paragraph 2): {+2. IMMEDIATELY NOTIFYING LOCAL, STATE AND FEDERAL LAW ENFORCEMENT AUTHORITIES OF MULTIPLE HANDGUN PURCHASES BY THE SAME CUSTOMER THAT OCCUR WITHIN ANY NINETY-DAY PERIOD.+}
Sec. 1 (A.R.S. 44-7862, subsection G): {+G. A FIREARMS DEALER THAT TRANSFERS FIREARMS TO INDIVIDUALS SHALL MAINTAIN A LIABILITY INSURANCE POLICY WITH A MINIMUM POLICY LIMIT OF $1,000,000 TO COMPENSATE POTENTIAL VICTIMS FOR DAMAGE TO PROPERTY AND FOR INJURY TO OR DEATH OF ANY INDIVIDUAL AS A RESULT OF A FIREARMS DEALER'S WRONGFUL CONDUCT IN THE TRANSFER OF ANY FIREARM OR AMMUNITION.+}
